Exclude saturated and near-black RGB samples from software ISP white balance.
The OP6 rear cameras often clip green before red/blue; including those samples
underestimates the required red/blue gains and produces a strong green cast.
Retain the original all-pixel sums/histogram for AE and black-level estimation.
Normalize the dedicated AWB accumulator to eight bits before merging jobs,
subtract the measured black level, and keep the previous gains when fewer
than 64 safe samples remain. Preserve the existing 4x gain limit.

